{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8c0f41b5-446a-49e2-8833-723d238c3f62","agentId":"ae2337b31e58469c0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are an independent, adversarial VERIFIER for a gauntlet review of a game-engine skill framework (a self-contained capability map, skill hierarchy, contracts, radar, legacy catalogue, milestones, untrusted-input registry; it has no relation to other skills). Data under /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r3/engine-skill-framework (read only inside that directory; data/*.json is the source of truth; the docstring at the top of scripts/check.py lists what is machine-proved; you may run `python3 scripts/check.py`).\nInput: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/verify_in_K-SEC.json — 17 findings by the Security critic.\nFor EACH finding, judge it independently (do not let neighbouring findings sway you; default to holds=false if you cannot confirm):\n- FACT: does the deficiency exist as described in the data (ids exist/missing as claimed; nothing already covers it under another name, e.g. XC.SEC.*, untrusted-inputs.json entries; check.py does not already prove it)? Name the ids/files you checked.\n- MATERIALITY: is it a real, material defect for a framework coordinating autonomous agents (not style; not contradicting a recorded, reasoned scope decision in docs/06 section C or docs/00 without new evidence); is the proposed change sound? Is the severity right?\nWrite results as JSON to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/verify_out_K-SEC.json: a list of {\"id\",\"fact_holds\":bool,\"material\":bool,\"severity_ok\":bool,\"checked\":\"ids/files you inspected\",\"reason\":\"one or two sentences\"} — exactly one entry per input finding. Final message: one line with counts of confirmed (both true) findings."},"uuid":"86781d39-5e8e-4b38-ad04-b73c6be49336","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:19:42.145Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
