\"untrusted-inputs.json\") if os.path.exists(os.path.join(DATA, \"untrusted-inputs.json\")) else {\"inputs\": []}\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:173:| assets | serialization-schema | package-formats-vfs | hostile-local | harness | size/depth/count |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:179:| saves | persistence-save | serialization-schema | trusted-local | harness | size/depth |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:180:| cloud-saves | persistence-save | — | semi-trusted-signed | harness | size/depth |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:181:| scripts | scripting-runtime | — | hostile-local | harness | time/memory/instructions |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:182:| mods | modding-ugc | plugin-system | hostile-local | harness | size/permissions |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:185:| remote-config | online-services-liveops | — | semi-trusted-signed | harness | size/keys |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:187:| fonts | text-fonts | — | hostile-local | harness | tables/glyphs |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:188:| media-decoders | media-playback | — | hostile-local | harness | resolution/duration |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:189:| decompressors | containers-core-types | package-formats-vfs | hostile-local | harness | ratio/output size |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:192:| editor-plugins | plugin-system | — | hostile-local | harness | permissions |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:193:| imported-dcc-files | asset-import-interchange | — | hostile-local | harness | size/depth |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:195:| admin-commands | dedicated-server | — | semi-trusted-signed | harness | rate/RBAC |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:196:| automation-commands | visual-debugging-tools | editor-architect | hostile-local | harness | dev-only/auth |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:201:| ml-models | ml-inference-runtime | — | semi-trusted-signed | harness | size/op set |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:204:| collab-session | collaboration-version-control | — | hostile-local | harness | size/rate |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:205:| shared-ddc | content-pipeline-architect | — | hostile-local | harness | content-addressed/verified |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:206:| dcc-live-link | asset-import-interchange | — | hostile-local | harness | rate/size |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:207:| procedural-asset-eval | asset-import-interchange | — | hostile-local | harness | sandboxed out-of-process |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:208:| launch-args | core-runtime-architect | platform-mobile, platform-desktop, platform-console | hostile-local | harness | allow-listed settable-from layers |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:209:| config-layers | core-runtime-architect | — | semi-trusted-signed | harness | trust tier per layer |\n## C. Known coverage weaknesses of this framework itself\n\nThese are admitted limits of phase 1 that critics should keep testing:\n\n1. **Parameters behind NDAs.** Console-specific skills can be *structured* now but not *filled*. Phase 2 must mark console content as \"requires licensed platform documentation\".\n2. **Game-specific systems.** Quest *content*, inventory rules and economy design are game code on top of `C-GAME`. Round 1 moved some of this territory into the engine: the dialogue line model and narrative state (`narrative-dialogue`), designer data (`gameplay-data`) and character movement (`character-movement`), because each carries formats shared across four or more engine domains. The boundary may still be challenged per genre.\n3. **Backend services.** Backend services are outside engine scope by decision (`engine-architect` non-goal register). The engine owns only the integration boundary, the server process lifecycle (`C-SERVER`) and server artifacts.\n4. **Membership is \"may be built\", not \"must be built\".** A configuration's members are the skills available to it; a game built on that configuration uses a subset. Milestones therefore prove availability, and the reference game of each configuration proves use.\n5. **Critic misses.** Round 2 critics missed three planted seeds in their own mandates (continuous collision, lag compensation, golden-image tests). Those critics are on a first strike (PROTOCOL.md).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3078f5a1-cb36-4959-89e7-1ce614db31ef","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:20:09.161Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d263499-be8c-46c0-9b8a-44f1c9c0c14d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
