{"parentUuid":"a0805b3c-24c3-4490-a9c3-daad07186019","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8c0f41b5-446a-49e2-8833-723d238c3f62","agentId":"ae2337b31e58469c0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017MCEH7e8LF2B167DmaEkmf","type":"tool_result","content":"scripts/check.py:35:  * every code contract has an oracle author other than its sole implementer; boundary contracts declare a\nscripts/check.py:523:    # -- oracle independence and verified test doubles\nscripts/check.py:528:        oa = c.get(\"oracle_author\")\nscripts/check.py:530:            E(f\"code contract {cid} has no valid oracle_author\")\nscripts/check.py:532:            E(f\"code contract {cid}: its sole implementer {oa} is also its oracle author\")\nscripts/check.py:630:        (\"implementer grades itself\", lambda m: m.contract(\"C-NAV\").__setitem__(\"oracle_author\", \"navigation-pathfinding\"), \"is also its oracle author\"),\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:35:**Workstreams** (foundation, platform, content, world, rendering, simulation, audio, online, gameplay, UI, tools, release, quality, performance, governance, assurance) group skills for delegated arbitration and staffing. They are also the co-hosting unit, so the independence matrix (`data/crosscutting.json`: decider vs reviewer, builder vs adjudicator, implementer v\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:102:| Instrumentation, tests, budgets and determinism levels exist before features (milestone gates from M0). Every code contract has an oracle author who is not its sole implementer; acceptance suites are read-only for implementers and have sealed holdouts. | Profiling and testing added late; implementers grading their own tests. | Performance claims need measurement,\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:124:| Validation of agent-produced work is owned separately (`QA.AGENT.*`): independent oracles, governed baselines, detection of weakened tests, and mutation gates. | Implementers must not control the oracles that judge them. |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:128:| Test infrastructure that ships as code is `test-runtime-harness` (`C-TESTHOST`, universal); strategy stays with `test-architect`. Every code contract names an oracle author. | Test runners and fault points must build on every target; implementers must not write the suites that judge them. |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:62:| Validation of autonomous-agent development (test side) | emerging | test-architect | `QA.AGENT.oracle-independence`, `QA.AGENT.baseline-governance`, `QA.AGENT.test-integrity`, `QA.AGENT.mutation-gate` | docs/06 A13; reward-hacking reports in agentic coding (2025) | Measured seeded-defect escape rate below threshold across N milestones | Mandatory human revie\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:63:| Governance of autonomous-agent development (review side) | emerging | architecture-governance | `ARCH.ORG.critic-calibration`, `ARCH.ORG.adjudication` | docs/06 A13; LLM-as-judge bias literature | Calibrated critic recall and precision stable across three milestones | Mandatory human review sampling per tier (ARCH.ORG.human-gates) and frozen agent authority \ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:64:| Agent provenance & boundaries | emerging | program-orchestration | `ARCH.ORG.provenance` | SLSA provenance applied to agents (new) | Industry provenance standard for AI-authored code | Mandatory human review sampling per tier (ARCH.ORG.human-gates) and frozen agent authority over oracles |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:65:| Development-agent security boundary | emerging | security-engineering | `XC.SEC.agent-boundary`, `XC.SEC.agent-redteam` | OWASP LLM01; CVE-2025-53773, CVE-2025-54135 | Demonstrated robust prompt-injection defence | Mandatory human review sampling per tier (ARCH.ORG.human-gates) and frozen agent authority over oracles |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:164:| L56 | Late or implementer-owned validation | tests written after features by their implementer | Oracles by declared oracle authors, tests before features | test-architect | `QA.AGENT.oracle-independence`, `QA.STRAT.dod` |\ndocs/09-radar-legacy-milestones.md:165:| L57 | Wall-clock time and exact-pixel goldens in tests | sleeps, real clocks, bit-exact images across GPUs | Injectable clocks, perceptual metrics with per-GPU tolerances | test-architect | `QA.STRAT.oracles`, `CORE.FRAME.test-clock` |\n{\n \"id\": \"C-SER\",\n \"layer\": 2,\n \"owner\": \"serialization-schema\",\n \"name\": \"Serialization & schema evolution\",\n \"summary\": \"Formats, versioning, upgraders, canonical form, untrusted-input rules.\",\n \"requires\": [\n  \"C-REFL\"\n ],\n \"conformance\": true,\n \"oracle_author\": \"collaboration-version-control\"\n}\n{\n \"id\": \"C-SIGN\",\n \"layer\": 1,\n \"owner\": \"security-runtime\",\n \"name\": \"Crypto & signed artifacts\",\n \"summary\": \"Crypto primitives and CSPRNG, signature envelope, trust roots, rotation/revocation, version floors (anti-rollback), algorithm agility.\",\n \"requires\": [\n  \"C-TYPES\"\n ],\n \"conformance\": true,\n \"oracle_author\": \"modding-ugc\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ac4e8295-d017-46d6-a419-1a7b15917fba","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:20:33.088Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a0805b3c-24c3-4490-a9c3-daad07186019","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
