{"parentUuid":"fb082ae3-d357-4769-9b2a-5b3c5be384c5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae2337b31e58469c0","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZDn5SoMeTC1duVxxf6h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1179,"cache_read_input_tokens":113403,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1179,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfZDn4yGApzsPESuurvew","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f9ab6a20-b60c-4abf-bde0-336f07fc0582","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:22:03.977Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"f9ab6a20-b60c-4abf-bde0-336f07fc0582","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae2337b31e58469c0","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZDn5SoMeTC1duVxxf6h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EuBTcEQhRoRNKKaUgjeaFL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nR=[\n(\"K-SEC-1\",1,1,0,\"untrusted-inputs.json saves/cloud-saves/config-layers; GAM.SAVE.integrity; docs/09\",\"saves is trusted-local, cloud-saves/config-layers semi-trusted-signed; user-editable saves are attacker-controlled, so label is wrong. But saves stay registered with a fuzz harness and size/depth limits and the trust field is not consumed by check.py, so nothing is exempted: minor, not major.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-2\",1,1,1,\"capabilities.json BLD.REL.staged-rollout; BLD.REL.rollback; legacy-patterns; milestones M4 gate\",\"Capability is literally defined as simultaneous global rollout with post-release kill switches; no phased/cohort/auto-halt capability exists anywhere. The M4 gate rests on it; the wording bakes in an all-at-once anti-pattern.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-3\",1,1,1,\"CNT.COOK.ddc, CNT.COOK.shared-cache, BLD.SYS.caching, RND.SHADER.cache, untrusted-inputs shared-ddc/shader-caches\",\"CNT.COOK.ddc is keyed by path+mtime, contradicting shared-ddc limit 'content-addressed/verified'; no compile-cache or trusted-writer rule is registered. Real cache-poisoning/supply-chain gap.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-4\",1,1,1,\"contracts.json C-SIGN/C-SER/C-SCRIPT; milestones.json freeze vs skill staffing; check.py oracle checks\",\"Recomputed: 29 contracts are frozen before their oracle author's first milestone; C-SIGN frozen M0 with modding-ugc (M4) as oracle author, and check.py only checks oracle != sole implementer. A crypto contract with a UGC skill as oracle author is a real defect.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-5\",1,1,1,\"skills.json workstreams; crosscutting.json independence; check.py independence loop; docs/00 workstreams\",\"security-runtime and security-engineering are both workstream 'quality', the co-hosting unit; the (security-engineering, owning-skill) pair is skipped by the workstream check. Reviewer/author independence for crypto code is unenforced.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-6\",0,0,0,\"skills.json keys (access only NDA); XC.SEC.agent-boundary; ARCH.ORG.human-gates; XC.SEC.agent-redteam\",\"Agent capability scoping, egress and prompt-injection model are already owned by XC.SEC.agent-boundary and CI/secret-scope changes are a human gate. A per-skill access schema plus a trifecta lint is a design preference for phase-2 SKILL.md, not a demonstrated defect.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-7\",1,1,1,\"untrusted-inputs.json (external-reports, vuln-reports, logged-untrusted-strings, crash-uploads); XC.SEC.agent-redteam; ARCH.ORG.change-requests; OBS.CRASH.feedback\",\"No registry entry for CI/test output, inter-agent change requests/messages or player feedback read by triage agents; external-reports covers customer intake only. Agent-to-agent injection propagation is a real uncovered path.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-8\",1,0,0,\"untrusted-inputs project-content-to-llm; ED.ARCH.llm-agent-frontend (emerging); ED.ARCH.automation-security; milestones.json\",\"Owner is ai-assisted-authoring (M6) as claimed, but the front end is an emerging capability with CLI fallback and milestones stage skills, not capabilities; editor-architect already owns workspace-trust/permission gating. No evidence the exposure exists at M2, and the input owner being the feature owner is defensible.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-9\",1,1,1,\"milestones.json M0-M2 skills and gates; skills.json kinds of ci-cd-automation/build-system-toolchains; XC.SEC.* caps\",\"ci-cd-automation and build-system-toolchains first appear at M2 while M0 exit claims CI lanes; no milestone gates supply-chain, agent-boundary, secrets, key-custody, data-rights, childrens-data or vuln-response (only threats, hardening, sandbox). Store-facing M2 has only QA.CERT.prechecks.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-10\",1,1,1,\"capabilities BLD.CI.*, BLD.SYS.*, XC.SEC.supply-chain, BLD.REL.server-artifacts, NET.SRV.*\",\"No capability for build provenance, hermetic/ephemeral runners, untrusted-vs-privileged job separation, OIDC identity or server secret delivery; XC.SEC.supply-chain lists only build-system-toolchains as contributor and ci-cd-automation has no security capability. Partly overlapped by XC.SEC.secrets/key-custody but the core gap stands.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-11\",1,1,1,\"crosscutting.json concerns (30, none on personal data); XC.SEC.data-rights, XC.SEC.privacy-review\",\"No concern makes each skill declare personal data collected/logged/sent; privacy-review and data-rights need that input, and concerns are the framework's mechanism for SKILL.md obligations.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-12\",1,0,0,\"untrusted-inputs editor-plugins; XC.EXT.plugin-trust; XC.SEC.dev-trust; ED.ARCH.process; XC.EXT.mod-editor\",\"Plugin signing, workspace trust and sandboxed tool plugins are already covered by XC.SEC.dev-trust and XC.EXT.mod-editor; ED.ARCH.process decides in/out-of-process. Remaining issue is wording of a manifest field, not a material omission.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-13\",1,1,1,\"PLAT.COMM.*, PLAT.SVC.identity/entitlements, NET.SRV.transactions, untrusted-inputs\",\"No refund/void/revocation/clawback capability and no store-notification input; PLAT.SVC.identity mentions account linking but nothing on secure login flow or token storage. Refund abuse is a real integration-boundary hole; token/PKCE parts are weaker.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-14\",1,1,1,\"capabilities PLAT.WEB.runtime; CORE.JOBS.degenerate\",\"Text literally says cross-origin isolation is assumed on every host, which is false for portal iframes; CORE.JOBS.degenerate (with platform-web) already gives the fallback that the capability fails to reference. Wrong assumption in the web runtime.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-15\",0,0,0,\"XC.SEC.tamper; XC.SEC.hardening; XC.SEC.anticheat; docs/00\",\"XC.SEC.tamper is a policy/boundary capability of security-engineering like XC.SEC.hardening, with build/package implementation under BLD.REL.packaging; ownership is a defensible choice and the process-skill rule concerns code, not policy.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-16\",1,1,1,\"skills.json security-engineering purpose/expertise/non_responsibilities; XC.SEC.privacy owner\",\"Purpose and expertise still say privacy engineering though XC.SEC.privacy is owned by privacy-data-protection, and non_responsibilities omit privacy and crypto code routing. Small text fix, correctly minor.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-17\",1,1,1,\"BLD.CI.build-distribution; BLD.SYS.dev-surface-exclusion; BLD.REL.preload-embargo\",\"Build distribution has no dev-surface, watermarking or revocation requirement; dev-surface exclusion is scoped to shipping configurations. Small but real gap for external builds.\"),\n]\nout=[{\"id\":i,\"fact_holds\":bool(f),\"material\":bool(m),\"severity_ok\":bool(s),\"checked\":c,\"reason\":r} for i,f,m,s,c,r in R]\njson.dump(out,open('verify_out_K-SEC.json','w'),indent=1)\nprint(len(out),sum(o['fact_holds'] and o['material'] for o in out))\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1179,"cache_read_input_tokens":113403,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1179,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EuBTcEQhRoRNKKaUgjeaFL":{"command":"cd /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nR=[\n(\"K-SEC-1\",1,1,0,\"untrusted-inputs.json saves/cloud-saves/config-layers; GAM.SAVE.integrity; docs/09\",\"saves is trusted-local, cloud-saves/config-layers semi-trusted-signed; user-editable saves are attacker-controlled, so label is wrong. But saves stay registered with a fuzz harness and size/depth limits and the trust field is not consumed by check.py, so nothing is exempted: minor, not major.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-2\",1,1,1,\"capabilities.json BLD.REL.staged-rollout; BLD.REL.rollback; legacy-patterns; milestones M4 gate\",\"Capability is literally defined as simultaneous global rollout with post-release kill switches; no phased/cohort/auto-halt capability exists anywhere. The M4 gate rests on it; the wording bakes in an all-at-once anti-pattern.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-3\",1,1,1,\"CNT.COOK.ddc, CNT.COOK.shared-cache, BLD.SYS.caching, RND.SHADER.cache, untrusted-inputs shared-ddc/shader-caches\",\"CNT.COOK.ddc is keyed by path+mtime, contradicting shared-ddc limit 'content-addressed/verified'; no compile-cache or trusted-writer rule is registered. Real cache-poisoning/supply-chain gap.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-4\",1,1,1,\"contracts.json C-SIGN/C-SER/C-SCRIPT; milestones.json freeze vs skill staffing; check.py oracle checks\",\"Recomputed: 29 contracts are frozen before their oracle author's first milestone; C-SIGN frozen M0 with modding-ugc (M4) as oracle author, and check.py only checks oracle != sole implementer. A crypto contract with a UGC skill as oracle author is a real defect.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-5\",1,1,1,\"skills.json workstreams; crosscutting.json independence; check.py independence loop; docs/00 workstreams\",\"security-runtime and security-engineering are both workstream 'quality', the co-hosting unit; the (security-engineering, owning-skill) pair is skipped by the workstream check. Reviewer/author independence for crypto code is unenforced.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-6\",0,0,0,\"skills.json keys (access only NDA); XC.SEC.agent-boundary; ARCH.ORG.human-gates; XC.SEC.agent-redteam\",\"Agent capability scoping, egress and prompt-injection model are already owned by XC.SEC.agent-boundary and CI/secret-scope changes are a human gate. A per-skill access schema plus a trifecta lint is a design preference for phase-2 SKILL.md, not a demonstrated defect.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-7\",1,1,1,\"untrusted-inputs.json (external-reports, vuln-reports, logged-untrusted-strings, crash-uploads); XC.SEC.agent-redteam; ARCH.ORG.change-requests; OBS.CRASH.feedback\",\"No registry entry for CI/test output, inter-agent change requests/messages or player feedback read by triage agents; external-reports covers customer intake only. Agent-to-agent injection propagation is a real uncovered path.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-8\",1,0,0,\"untrusted-inputs project-content-to-llm; ED.ARCH.llm-agent-frontend (emerging); ED.ARCH.automation-security; milestones.json\",\"Owner is ai-assisted-authoring (M6) as claimed, but the front end is an emerging capability with CLI fallback and milestones stage skills, not capabilities; editor-architect already owns workspace-trust/permission gating. No evidence the exposure exists at M2, and the input owner being the feature owner is defensible.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-9\",1,1,1,\"milestones.json M0-M2 skills and gates; skills.json kinds of ci-cd-automation/build-system-toolchains; XC.SEC.* caps\",\"ci-cd-automation and build-system-toolchains first appear at M2 while M0 exit claims CI lanes; no milestone gates supply-chain, agent-boundary, secrets, key-custody, data-rights, childrens-data or vuln-response (only threats, hardening, sandbox). Store-facing M2 has only QA.CERT.prechecks.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-10\",1,1,1,\"capabilities BLD.CI.*, BLD.SYS.*, XC.SEC.supply-chain, BLD.REL.server-artifacts, NET.SRV.*\",\"No capability for build provenance, hermetic/ephemeral runners, untrusted-vs-privileged job separation, OIDC identity or server secret delivery; XC.SEC.supply-chain lists only build-system-toolchains as contributor and ci-cd-automation has no security capability. Partly overlapped by XC.SEC.secrets/key-custody but the core gap stands.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-11\",1,1,1,\"crosscutting.json concerns (30, none on personal data); XC.SEC.data-rights, XC.SEC.privacy-review\",\"No concern makes each skill declare personal data collected/logged/sent; privacy-review and data-rights need that input, and concerns are the framework's mechanism for SKILL.md obligations.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-12\",1,0,0,\"untrusted-inputs editor-plugins; XC.EXT.plugin-trust; XC.SEC.dev-trust; ED.ARCH.process; XC.EXT.mod-editor\",\"Plugin signing, workspace trust and sandboxed tool plugins are already covered by XC.SEC.dev-trust and XC.EXT.mod-editor; ED.ARCH.process decides in/out-of-process. Remaining issue is wording of a manifest field, not a material omission.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-13\",1,1,1,\"PLAT.COMM.*, PLAT.SVC.identity/entitlements, NET.SRV.transactions, untrusted-inputs\",\"No refund/void/revocation/clawback capability and no store-notification input; PLAT.SVC.identity mentions account linking but nothing on secure login flow or token storage. Refund abuse is a real integration-boundary hole; token/PKCE parts are weaker.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-14\",1,1,1,\"capabilities PLAT.WEB.runtime; CORE.JOBS.degenerate\",\"Text literally says cross-origin isolation is assumed on every host, which is false for portal iframes; CORE.JOBS.degenerate (with platform-web) already gives the fallback that the capability fails to reference. Wrong assumption in the web runtime.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-15\",0,0,0,\"XC.SEC.tamper; XC.SEC.hardening; XC.SEC.anticheat; docs/00\",\"XC.SEC.tamper is a policy/boundary capability of security-engineering like XC.SEC.hardening, with build/package implementation under BLD.REL.packaging; ownership is a defensible choice and the process-skill rule concerns code, not policy.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-16\",1,1,1,\"skills.json security-engineering purpose/expertise/non_responsibilities; XC.SEC.privacy owner\",\"Purpose and expertise still say privacy engineering though XC.SEC.privacy is owned by privacy-data-protection, and non_responsibilities omit privacy and crypto code routing. Small text fix, correctly minor.\"),\n(\"K-SEC-17\",1,1,1,\"BLD.CI.build-distribution; BLD.SYS.dev-surface-exclusion; BLD.REL.preload-embargo\",\"Build distribution has no dev-surface, watermarking or revocation requirement; dev-surface exclusion is scoped to shipping configurations. Small but real gap for external builds.\"),\n]\nout=[{\"id\":i,\"fact_holds\":bool(f),\"material\":bool(m),\"severity_ok\":bool(s),\"checked\":c,\"reason\":r} for i,f,m,s,c,r in R]\njson.dump(out,open('verify_out_K-SEC.json','w'),indent=1)\nprint(len(out),sum(o['fact_holds'] and o['material'] for o in out))\nE"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfZDn4yGApzsPESuurvew","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"26937229-6ee8-4325-a47e-e48265e8f381","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:22:22.353Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
